+flow's end wrote, and the files it names, each by its sha256. A stats run holds the edit's small
+files under edit/, copied when it began, so one folder answers the whole report; an edit run
+answers what the edit made and leaves the statistics missing, saying they wait for the stats stage.
+The two stages are two GPU jobs, which may run on other nodes, cards and commits, so what a job ran
+on is said job by job, each from the files that job wrote: the edit's from its record and its
+inputs.json, the stats job's from its own record and environment.json.
+
+A code answer reads only those files and the frozen design, never infers, and is missing where a
+file is absent or no longer the bytes the record names. The owner asked on 2026-10-29 at 03:35 UTC,
+of the DRR study's report, "why would I answer these question instead of having a real meta flow
+run generate them?", so every item the study's own files answer is answered here; an answer that
+restates the frozen design (PREREG.md, DEVIATIONS.md, README.md) holds only for a run whose records
+name that design's bytes, DESIGN, so a second design is never reported in this one's words. What no
+file says is the owner's, in data/reporting/studies/flux-realism.json, into which a session copies
+only the owner's own words. The study trains no network: an item about a trained model is answered
